For anyone with an idea and no team yet.

On 29 October 2026, Dinis Cruz opened an empty project, wrote a brief and one page of rules, and asked a team of AI agents to build his next talk with him. Nine agents joined, each with one job written down. That evening, nineteen hours after the first commit, he gave the talk.

This book follows that day as a factory: who did what, and when; the five stages the team ran on its turns, with the plan and the work each checked; the one short file anyone could use to stop everything, and that only he could lift; and what did not work, because that is in the book too.

The scenes are dramatised and marked as such. The events, and every number, rest on a record you can check.

Then it is your turn: one agent, one page of rules in your own words, one brief, and one small, finished piece of work on the first day.

Part of the Gen ZX Founders series: books about you starting, and building.

